    "result_text": "All tests pass. The change is complete and green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `namesakeCount` \u2014 the number of existing owners sharing the same first and last name (case-insensitively) at the time an owner is created \u2014 placing each piece of logic where it belongs:\n\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `namesakeCount` integer to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field and MapStruct maps it automatically (no mapper changes needed).\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added the `namesake_count`-backed `Integer namesakeCount` field with its getter/setter, alongside the other owner attributes.\n- **`ClinicService` / `ClinicServiceImpl`** \u2014 Added `countNamesakes(firstName, lastName)`, reusing the existing `findByLastNameIgnoreCase` repository method (the same query the household logic already uses) and filtering on first name case-insensitively. This keeps the count logic in the service layer, not the controller.\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 Computes and stamps the count onto the owner just before persisting, so it reflects the state *before* this create.\n- **Schema files** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 Added the `namesake_count` column so the value persists and is read back on `GET`.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreCountsNamesakes` and the full suite both pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
